# Horwall example patterns
# Review before enabling bans: rules for login pages, MCP/GraphQL endpoints,
# PHP and config files can match legitimate application routes.
# Remove or narrow them for your site.
# One regex per line. Positive rules match only the request path, without query strings.
#
# Anchor rules to path segments to avoid matching inside words:
#   (^|/)name    "name" starts a path segment
#   (/|$)        end of a segment
# For example, plain "sse" also matches /assets/ and /tags/dnssec/, and plain
# "config" matches /tags/ispconfig/: both are legitimate pages.
#
# Exclusions: prefix a regex with ! to allow matching request paths.
# They take precedence over ALL positive rules, regardless of file order.
# Only the path is checked: query strings are ignored, Referer/User-Agent
# cannot grant an exclusion. Paths are not URL-decoded or normalized.
# Use ^ and $ for an exact path, and \. for a literal dot.
#
# Example: uncomment to allow /allowed.php (also /allowed.php?x=1).
# /other/allowed.php and /allowed.php/extra would NOT be exempt.
# Other PHP paths still match the positive PHP rule below.
# This prevents notifications for this request; it does not lift existing bans.
# !^/allowed\.php$
#
# A bare ! is invalid. Use [!] to match a literal leading ! in a positive rule.
# Restart Horwall after changing the installed pattern file.
#
# No positive rules specifically for these names (NOT explicit exclusions):
# robots.txt
# sitemap.xml
# favicon.ico
# logo.png
# /.well-known/   (dotfile rules below list names explicitly to spare it)

# --- Explicit exclusions (always allowed, override every rule below)
!^/ads\.txt$

# --- WordPress and other CMS probes
^/wp-
(^|/)wp-(admin|content|includes|json|login|config)
^/(wordpress|wp)(/|$)
^/administrator(/|$)
(^|/)admin/controller/extension

# --- Server-side scripts (remove if your site runs PHP, CGI, Java, ASP)
\.(php[0-9]?|phtml|phar)
\.(aspx?|jsp|action|do|cgi)(/|$)
(^|/)cgi-bin(/|$)
(^|/)phpinfo
xleet

# --- Dotfiles: VCS, environment, credentials, tool settings
\.env([._~/-]|$)
(^|/)\.(git|svn|hg|bzr)(/|$|[a-z_-])
(^|/)\.(aws|AWS_|ssh|docker|kube|cursor|claude|vscode|idea|composer|cargo|terraform|vault-token|boto|amplifyrc|npmrc|netrc|pgpass|my\.cnf|htpasswd|htaccess|DS_Store|bash_history)
(^|/)\.\.(/|$)

# --- Config, secrets, state and backup files
(^|[/._-])config\.(json|xml|ya?ml|js|ts|inc|bak|old)$
(^|/)kube/config$
^/((api|v[0-9]|admin)/)?config(/|$)
(^|[/._-])(credentials|secrets)(\.[a-z]+)?$
terraform\.tfstate
(^|/)docker-compose[^/]*\.ya?ml$
(^|/)environment[^/]*\.ts$
(^|/)storage/logs/
(^|/)backup[^/]*\.(zip|tar|gz|tgz|7z|rar|sql)$
\.(sql|bak|swp)(\.(gz|zip))?$

# --- Admin and API endpoints (remove if your site exposes them)
^/([a-z_-]+/)?login(\.[a-z]+)?/?$
^/(api/)?(mcp|sse)(/|$)
^/(api/)?graphql(/|$)
(^|/)(actuator|server-status)(/|$)

# --- Aggressive (uncomment only if these paths never exist on your sites)
# ^/(old|new|bk|bc|backup|bak)/?$
